ultra-fast-lzma2 v1.6.2 (tag v1.6.2, commit bd4682f, 2026-10-09). Its decoder now
rejects an LZMA chunk that completes its output without consuming its whole packed
size, as the LZMA SDK does; compressed bytes are the same as 1.6.1, 1.6.0 and
1.5.1. 1.6.1 (0d920cb), the stability release, fixed two more decoder defects (a
corrupt chunk could make it read up to 20 bytes past its input, and a chunk without
properties after a dictionary reset was accepted with pb uninitialized, which
crashed the assembler decoder). 1.6.0 (f4f5dba) added .xz streaming features
zpaq-std does not use; 1.5.1 (a19bae2) fixed the 32-bit Windows crash of 1.5.0
(hardware CRC run on threads Windows creates without realigning the stack); do not
go back to 1.5.0.
Source: https://github.com/YadeWira/ultra-fast-lzma2, a fork of Conor McCarthy's
fast-lzma2 (most of the code is his). Dual licensed BSD / GPLv2; zpaq-std uses it
under the BSD license, see LICENSE.
Files copied unmodified: the library's *.c and *.h, lzma_dec_x86_64.S and
lzma_dec_arm64.S (the LZMA SDK's assembler decoders, public domain), LICENSE.
(Not copied: the MASM lzma_dec_x86_64.asm, bench/, dll/, fuzzer/, test/, tools/.)

Used by zpaq-std -ma:uflzma2 through UF2_compress, UF2_compressBound,
UF2_maxCLevel and UF2_decompress only; blocks carry the ZPAQUFLZMA2 decoder.
Built next to compressors/fl2 (fast-lzma2 1.0.1, -ma:flzma2): the two share
internal symbol names (LZMA2_*, RMF_*, xxhash...), so the Makefile links this
library into one relocatable object (ld -r) and renames every global symbol but
UF2_* with a ufl2_ prefix (objcopy --redefine-syms, the list taken from nm).
Making them local instead, as the library's bench/lzbench/add_uflzma2.py does,
works on Linux but not on Windows x64: the COMDAT ".refptr.price_table" section
both libraries carry is kept once for the two, and uf-lzma2 crashed.
The assembler decoder is linked on x86_64 (MS_x64_CALL=1 on Windows) and ARM64,
with -DLZMA2_DEC_OPT; 32-bit builds use the C decoder.
Do not patch these files here: send changes to the ultra-fast-lzma2 repository.
